    "how_to_read": "the noise curve is single-drive work made progressively harder to read. If a mixture arm sits ABOVE that curve at the same goal accuracy, the extra breadth is diversity rather than difficulty, and purpose_breadth is a usable signal. If it sits on the curve, breadth cannot tell 'many drives' from 'hard to read' and Sounding Line cannot use it as a motivational measure."
